1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Public AMM orders expose size and slippage.
ShadowSwap moves that exposure boundary.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Amount in and minimum out stay encrypted as iExec Nox handles
while the intent waits in the book.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Same-pair intents share a batch window.
The solver performs one public AMM swap.

4
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Each user’s output is immediately re-shielded
into a confidential token balance.

5
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Live proof: two intents, 5 + 7 sUSD,
one successful 12 sUSD AMM transaction.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The output split pro rata into two confidential cSETH balances.
The public AMM leg remains visible.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Pre-trade privacy. Batch obfuscation. Selective auditor access.
Private balances after settlement.

8
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Live Sepolia evidence is ready for review.
